    "token_sent_in_body": true,
    "token_in_path_or_query": false,
    "stored_anywhere": false,
    "logged": false,
    "rationale": "The token arrives in the address bar, so this is the one place the value is somewhere the user can see, a browser can remember, and an extension can read. It is read and the entry that carried it is overwritten in the same operation, before the value reaches any caller, so no caller can fail in a way that leaves it on screen. Replacement is used and never a push: a pushed entry would leave the token in the back stack, where Back would restore it into the address bar long after the invitation was accepted."
